const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"公司相关与日期相关可能同时存在",en:"Firm and date dependence can coexist"},body:{zh:"同一公司的多个日期可能共享未观测因素，同一天的不同公司也可能受到共同冲击。只按公司聚类会漏掉后一类联系，只按日期聚类又会漏掉前一类。论文针对这种彼此交叉而非完全嵌套的相关结构建立协方差估计。",en:"A firm's observations can share persistent influences, while different firms share shocks on the same date. Clustering only by firm misses the latter; clustering only by date misses the former. The paper addresses these crossed, non-nested dependence structures."},reference:{url:"https://cameron.econ.ucdavis.edu/research/CGM_twoway_ALL_13may2008.pdf",label:{zh:"2008年5月作者稿 · §1",en:"May 2008 author manuscript · §1"}}},{title:{zh:"嵌套分组不必重复加一层",en:"Nested groups need not be counted twice"},body:{zh:"作者区分交叉聚类与嵌套聚类：如果较小的簇完全属于较大的簇，在适当条件下按较大层级聚类即可。家庭属于州和公司跨越日期是不同结构。选择聚类维度应从观测如何共享冲击出发，而不是机械增加标准误选项。",en:"The paper distinguishes crossed from nested clustering. When smaller clusters are entirely contained within larger ones, clustering at the larger level can suffice under the relevant assumptions. Household-within-state and firm-by-date structures therefore require different reasoning."},reference:{url:"https://cameron.econ.ucdavis.edu/research/CGM_twoway_ALL_13may2008.pdf",label:{zh:"2008年5月作者稿 · §1",en:"May 2008 author manuscript · §1"}}},{title:{zh:"不共享任何簇的观测仍有限制",en:"Observations sharing no cluster remain restricted"},body:{zh:"双向设定允许只要共享任一聚类维度的观测之间存在相关，却对两个维度都不共享的误差施加不相关条件。若不同公司、不同日期仍受持续共同冲击影响，这个条件可能失败。多维这个名字并不代表已经处理一切依赖。",en:"The two-way setup allows correlation when observations share either cluster dimension, but restricts errors sharing neither. Persistent common shocks across different firms and dates can violate that condition. Multiway does not mean that all possible dependence has been handled."},reference:{url:"https://cameron.econ.ucdavis.edu/research/CGM_twoway_ALL_13may2008.pdf",label:{zh:"2008年5月作者稿 · §2.2 · equation (2.12)",en:"May 2008 author manuscript · §2.2 · equation (2.12)"}}},{title:{zh:"两项相加，再减去交集",en:"Add both dimensions, subtract their intersection"},body:{zh:"双向估计把第一维和第二维的聚类协方差相加，再减去两维交集的聚类协方差，避免重复计算共享两维的观测对。交集是公司与日期等标签的联合组合，不是任选一维。三个组成部分必须基于同一回归与同一有效样本。",en:"The two-way estimator adds covariance estimates clustered on each dimension, then subtracts clustering on their intersection to avoid double counting. The intersection consists of joint labels. All three components must refer to the same regression and effective sample."},reference:{url:"https://cameron.econ.ucdavis.edu/research/CGM_twoway_ALL_13may2008.pdf",label:{zh:"2008年5月作者稿 · §2.2 · equations (2.14)–(2.15)",en:"May 2008 author manuscript · §2.2 · equations (2.14)–(2.15)"}}},{title:{zh:"关键是簇数，不只是记录数",en:"Cluster counts matter, not just row counts"},body:{zh:"理论要求各维的簇数增长，双向情形尤其关注较小的那个簇数。很多公司但只有少数年份，并不会因为总记录数很大就自动获得可靠推断。论文讨论有限样本修正，但这些修正不能把少数独立簇变成大量独立信息。",en:"The theory requires cluster counts to grow along each dimension, especially the smaller count in the two-way case. Many firms over very few years do not automatically provide reliable inference. Finite-sample adjustments cannot create independent information that is absent."},reference:{url:"https://cameron.econ.ucdavis.edu/research/CGM_twoway_ALL_13may2008.pdf",label:{zh:"2008年5月作者稿 · §1; §2.2",en:"May 2008 author manuscript · §1; §2.2"}}},{title:{zh:"多维修正也可能产生异常协方差",en:"Multiway correction can still produce problematic covariance"},body:{zh:"由于包含减法，有限样本估计可能出现负的方差项；作者明确讨论这一问题。扩展到三维时，需要按交集层级交替加减，而不是只把三张矩阵相加。发现异常结果应检查簇结构与样本条件，不能静默取绝对值掩盖。",en:"Subtraction can produce negative variance estimates in finite samples, a problem explicitly discussed in the manuscript. Three dimensions require alternating inclusion-exclusion terms. Problematic results call for inspecting cluster structure and sample conditions, not silently taking absolute values."},reference:{url:"https://cameron.econ.ucdavis.edu/research/CGM_twoway_ALL_13may2008.pdf",label:{zh:"2008年5月作者稿 · §2.2–2.3 · pp. 9–10",en:"May 2008 author manuscript · §2.2–2.3 · pp. 9–10"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"导读采用2008年作者稿。多维聚类不是允许所有观测任意相关；各维簇数、簇间依赖与有限样本协方差问题都影响推断。",en:"This guide uses the 2008 manuscript. Multiway clustering does not permit arbitrary dependence everywhere; cluster counts, between-cluster dependence and finite-sample covariance problems affect inference."}};export{e as default};
